[{:name "frontier-of-open-connected-component-lies-in-ambient-frontier"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Relate the ambient frontier of `connectedComponentIn U x` to the frontier of an open ambient subset `U` in a locally connected space."
   :statement
   "frontier (connectedComponentIn U x) ⊆ frontier U"
   :preconditions
   ["`LocallyConnectedSpace α`"
    "`IsOpen U`"
    "`x ∈ U`"]
   :proof-shape
   ["Use `hU.connectedComponentIn` to show the component is open, so its interior is itself."
    "The component is contained in `U`, hence closure monotonicity supplies the closure half of frontier membership."
    "Express the relative component as the image of `connectedComponent (⟨x,hx⟩ : U)` using `connectedComponentIn_eq_image hx`."
    "Use closedness/maximality of the connected component in the subtype to show `U ↓∩ connectedComponentIn U x` is relatively closed."
    "Transfer relative closedness with `isClosed_preimage_val.mp`; a putative frontier point lying in `U` would then lie back in the component, contradicting the frontier's non-interior half."]
   :key-api
   ["IsOpen.connectedComponentIn"
    "connectedComponentIn_subset"
    "connectedComponentIn_eq_image"
    "isClosed_connectedComponent"
    "isClosed_preimage_val"]
   :witness
   {:declaration
    "ConstructionTargets.LemniscateComponents.frontier_connectedComponentIn_subset_frontier"
    :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"]
    :sorryAx false}
   :boundary
   "This helper closes the ambient-frontier API gap only. It does not prove connectedness of the polynomial superlevel or count sublevel components."
   :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed}
